# Vulnerabilities reviewed and accepted for this image, not blanket-suppressed.
# Each entry below has no vendor-shipped fix available as of the scan date,
# and none of them apply to how this container actually runs (no privileged
# mount operations, no systemd-homed, no untrusted-symlink ACL handling).
# Re-run the scan periodically and drop any line here whose CVE gets a
# "Fixed Version" — at that point `apt-get upgrade` in the Dockerfile picks
# it up automatically and it should be fixed, not ignored.

# util-linux (CVE-2026-76642, -78408, -78409, -78410): mount-helper /
# nsenter / X-mount privilege-escalation issues. This image never invokes
# mount, nsenter, or any util-linux mount tooling — it's a Python web
# service, not a container runtime or init system.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# libacl1 (CVE-2026-54369): symlink traversal via libacl's ACL handling.
# Nothing in this codebase manipulates POSIX ACLs or follows
# attacker-controlled symlinks through libacl.
CVE-2026-54369

# libsystemd0 (CVE-2026-16742): local privilege escalation via
# systemd-homed. systemd-homed does not run inside this container (no
# systemd as PID 1, no homed service).
CVE-2026-16742
